        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dawn French, Jennifer Saunders, Al Pillay, Adrian Edmondson, Keith Allen, Nigel Planer, Alexei Sayle, Ronald Allen, Robbie Coltrane, Mandie Fletcher\n- Works: The Supergrass, French and Saunders, The Vicar of Dibley, Eat the Rich, The Comic Strip Presents, Gino, Absolutely Fabulous: The Movie, Absolutely Fabulous\n\nFacts:\n- Dawn Roma French was born on 11 October 1957 and is an English actress, writer, and comedian.\n- Dawn French is best known for starring in and writing for the comedy sketch show French and Saunders with Jennifer Saunders.\n- Dawn French also played the lead role of Geraldine Granger in the sitcom The Vicar of Dibley.\n- Alan \"Al\" Pillay was born on 22 August 1959 and is also known by the names Al Pillay, Alan Pellay, Alana Pellay, and Lana Pellay.\n- Al Pillay starred in Eat the Rich.\n- In The Comic Strip Presents, Al Pillay appeared as Alan Pellay playing Himself in the episode Gino and as Alana Pellay playing Herself in episode 13.\n- Al Pillay appeared as Lana Pellay playing Mary in the feature film The Supergrass.\n- The film The Supergrass starred Richardson, Adrian Edmondson, Jennifer Saunders, Dawn French, Keith Allen, Nigel Planer, Alexei Sayle, Ronald Allen, and Robbie Coltrane.\n- Absolutely Fabulous: The Movie is a 2016 British female buddy comedy film directed by Mandie Fletcher and written by Jennifer Saunders.\n- Absolutely Fabulous: The Movie was based on the television show Absolutely Fabulous.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
